NUM-22: do not carry a transect's meander adjustment into the next transect's n

transect_validate() multiplies the file-scope Nchannel by sqrt(Lfactor) to
build the transect's tables and leaves it that way. setManning() keeps the
current Nchannel when an NC line gives 0 for the channel ("no change from
previous NC line"), so the next transect inherited the previous transect's
meander-adjusted n. Restore the value as entered at the end of
transect_validate(); the tables and Transect[j].roughness are built exactly as
before.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply NUM-22_swmm530.patch

diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/transect.c b/src/legacy/engine/transect.c
index c8e58ca..5d930ec 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/transect.c
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/transect.c
@@ -259,6 +259,10 @@ void  transect_validate(int j)
 
     // --- save unadjusted main channel roughness 
     Transect[j].roughness = oldNchannel;
+
+    // --- restore it so that a following NC line with a zero channel n
+    //     inherits the value as entered, not the meander-adjusted one
+    Nchannel = oldNchannel;
 }
 
 //=============================================================================
